A||||6||Larry Pownall||Corvette vs Fiero||||12||
Z||000000||Larry Pownall||12-11-1999||12:47 PM||||My brother and I both own 88 GTs.  I live in Phoenix and he lives in Payson, AZ.  Payson is a small mountain town 80 miles from Phoenix.  His great mechanic, who loves my brother's showroom new 88 GT and now owns his own repair shop, told him about a time when he worked at the Chevy dealership in Payson during the 1980s.<P>GM has a test proving grounds near Phoenix.  The drivers use to stop in at the dealership in Payson when they would take cars out on the road.  One day two corvettes and a turbo powered Fiero stopped in at the Payson dealership.  The test drivers said....quote "this car will never make it into production, it out performs the corvettes in every way."<P>I had always heard the rumor that the corvette people were worried about the Fiero. However, I had never heard of actual statements made within GM.  Now I have!<P>I just had to share this story, received from a reliable source, with Fiero lovers.  I probably won't participate much in this forum||||reg||12
Z||000001||Monkeyman||12-11-1999||06:47 PM||||Why won't you participate much in this forum?  This is a GREAT place for info (there are some very smart people here!) and general talk about the cars we love.  Stick around for a while.  I'm sure you'll be glad you did.||||reg||1
Z||000002||william_thorniii||12-11-1999||09:14 PM||||I agree, if nothing else it is good to hear others with similar if albeit unhealthy obsessions.  Honestly though this forum is the best Fiero site that I have ever found.  Very informative and best of all friendly.  <P>Hey I have an idea!  The slogan for the Fiero should have been more like the one for Lays potato chips... Nobody can have just one... They truly are addictive.<P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||1
