Z||000005||Larry Pownall||12-12-1999||11:41 PM||||You seem like great guys.  Please don't think that my not participating much in the forum has anything to do with you.  I am just very busy and don't have a lot of extra time.<P>When I was told the story of the turbo Fiero yesterday......I just had to tell someone.  I went to a search engine looking for a Fiero discussion group and ended up here.<P>Because I love Fieros and know the story is true, I figured this story should be shared with other Fiero people.  I knew if I told anyone other than a Fiero fan their response would have been..."so what".<P>Yes, I believe, Payson does have a domed school as you described.  I will try to check into the forum once in awhile.||||reg||6
Z||000006||86_Fastback||12-14-1999||04:54 PM||||I have also talked to a GM person about fiero special projects.  I was told GM had an outside firm build 2 fiero structures out of aluminum.  In one of these, GM put in a turbo charged quad4.  Made the Corvette look like a slug.  ||||reg||1
